details:
(a) the State-wise/UT-wise number of Unique Disability ID (UDID) applications received, issued, rejected and pending since 2021;
(b) the State-wise/UT-wise grant-in-aid released for the Unique Disability Identification Project component of Scheme for Implementation of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (SIPDA) in each year since 2021;
(c) the average processing time for a UDID application, State-wise/UT-wise and the stage-wise pendency on the portal as on date; and
(d) the steps taken to improve the functioning of the UDID portal and to enhance central grant support for reducing pendency?

(a) the State/UT-wise number of Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana beneficiaries who availed no refill and who availed only one refill, in each year since 2021;
(b) the State/UT-wise per capita or per connection consumption of PMUY beneficiaries, in terms of the number of 14.2 kg cylinders taken per year since 2021, with the all-India figure;
(c) the State/UT-wise number of beneficiaries availing only one, only two and three or more refills annually since 2021, including the installation refill; and
(d) whether Government has assessed refill offtake under the Scheme and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of stations under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS) where works are completed, where works are in progress after award of tender and where tenders are yet to be awarded, State/UT-wise;
(b) the details for Karnataka, giving the sanctioned cost, year of sanction, date of award of contract and works completed for each, station-wise;
(c) the number of stations targeted for upgradation under the Scheme and the number actually upgraded in each year since its launch, year-wise; and
(d) the allocation and expenditure under Plan Head-53 'Customer Amenities' each year since launch, including South Western Railway, zone-wise?

(a) the State/UT-wise number of air quality monitoring stations operational in the country, as on date;
(b) the State/UT-wise financial assistance released under the National Air Quality Monitoring Programme for establishment, operation and maintenance of monitoring stations since 2021;
(c) the State/UT-wise number of non-attainment cities, the funds released to each under the National Clean Air Programme and the expenditure reported there under; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of monitoring network and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the State/UT-wise Central and District libraries set up, modernised or proposed under the National Mission on Libraries (NML) since inception;
(b) the year-wise budget allocated, funds released and expenditure incurred under the Mission;
(c) the State/UT-wise sanctioned posts, working strength and vacancies of librarians and staff;
(d) the State/UT-wise number of libraries digitised or under digitisation, including of manuscripts and books; and
(e) whether infrastructure gaps, staff shortages and digital access have been assessed and if so, the corrective measures taken thereon?

(a) the category-wise and State-wise/UT-wise total number of children, pregnant women and lactating women registered under Anganwadi services;
(b) State-wise/UT-wise number of beneficiaries whose e-KYC is pending, failed or could not be completed due to technical issues;
(c) State-wise/UT-wise and year-wise number of beneficiaries whose access to supplementary nutrition was delayed or denied due to Poshan Tracker-related issues since 2019; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure that eligible children, pregnant women and lactating mothers are not denied nutrition benefits under the scheme?

(a) the number of internship opportunities announced, applications received, candidates selected and internships completed under the Prime Minister Internship Scheme (PMIS) since its inception month-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of internship positions offered and filled under the Scheme company-wise;
(c) whether Government maintains data on employment outcomes of interns after completion of internship and if so, the number of interns who secured jobs or continued employment, social category-wise;
(d) the details of budget allocation, funds released and actual expenditure incurred under PMIS since inception year-wise; and
(e) whether Government has conducted any review regarding implementation gaps, low participation or drop-out rates under the Scheme?
